   "f:Skyrim.esm"
  ],
  "how": "peers are the rows of the same family, rank and tempering material; cost is how many materials a row asks, every input counted but gold coins. A row under low or over high times its peers' median cost has every material count multiplied by the one factor that brings it to the median, rounded, never under one. Every forge recipe that charges gold coins has them taken out (to 0). A row already listed keeps the original inputs it was first measured with."
